('B', '66339016-68a8-4fc0-b5fb-ee9ecfd13ac4', 'A8', 'The average rate of change from x=0 to x=2 is (0-4)/(2-0) which is -4/2, so the average rate is -2. I wasn''t really sure how to get the quadratic to fit all those numbers, like using ax^2+bx+c or something. And for the vertex, it''s like the turning point.', 'google', '{"content_key": "apprecalc-frq-001", "answer_type": "A8", "expected": [{"criterion_key": "part-a-criterion-1", "present": true}, {"criterion_key": "part-a-criterion-2", "present": false}, {"criterion_key": "part-b-criterion-1", "present": false}, {"criterion_key": "part-b-criterion-2", "present": false}, {"criterion_key": "part-c-criterion-1", "present": false}, {"criterion_key": "part-c-criterion-2", "present": false}]}'::jsonb, '30d97d6ebf5e76664097fdb974c406ee459ae07f15f303ffb30e27650c6dbccd', 'provisional_accept', 'daf64f87dc7cd511d5a501300c3457f6'),
('B', 'f514450c-4b28-4b3a-aaa4-e0fc7ac04796', 'A1', 'So first, the initial value is 12, and since the base is 1.18, that means it increases by 18% each unit of time.  

